<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Henry (VII) of Germany</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1211">1211</a>–<a href="/years/1242">1242</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> · Also known as Henry (VII), King of the Romans · Of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hohenstaufen">Hohenstaufen</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Henry (VII) was the eldest son of Emperor Frederick II and ruled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> as king from 1220 while his father lived in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>. In 1231 he bought the valley of Uri back from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburgs</a> and granted it imperial immediacy, a key step towards Swiss independence. He rebelled against his father, was deposed in 1235 and died in captivity in 1242.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/henry-vii-of-germany.jpg" alt="Henry (VII) of Germany" width="216" height="211" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Jindra7.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-more"><h2 class="enc-more-h">Early life and background</h2><p>Henry was born in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sicily">Sicily</a>, the only son of King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-ii">Frederick II</a> and his first wife Constance of Aragon, and was the elder brother of Conrad IV. While Frederick sought election as German king against Otto IV, he had his infant son crowned King of Sicily in March 1212 by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pope-innocent-iii">Pope Innocent III</a>. After the pope's death in 1216 Frederick called Henry to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> and entrusted him with the Duchy of Swabia. On 20 or 26 April 1220 the princes assembled at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frankfurt">Frankfurt</a> elected Henry King of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-empire">Romans</a>, in return for Frederick's confirmation of privileges to the prince-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishops</a>, but <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pope-honorius-iii">Pope Honorius III</a> did not recognise the election.</p><h2 class="enc-more-h">Reign</h2><p>After Frederick returned to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> in 1220, Henry was placed under the tutelage of Archbishop <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/engelbert-ii-of-berg">Engelbert I of Cologne</a>, who crowned him at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aachen">Aachen</a> on 8 May 1222. After Engelbert's death in 1225 Duke Louis I of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bavaria">Bavaria</a> took over the guardianship. On 29 November 1225 Henry married Margaret of Babenberg, daughter of Duke Leopold VI of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a>, they had two sons, Henry and Frederick, who both died young. Around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christmas">Christmas</a> 1228, after a falling-out with Louis of Bavaria, Henry took over the rule for himself.</p><p>The German princes, angered by his city-friendly policies, forced Henry to issue the Statutum in favorem principum at Worms on 1 May 1231, and their complaints turned Frederick against him. In 1233 and 1234 Henry angered his father again by intervening against the Archbishop of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bremen">Bremen</a>'s crusade against the peasants of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/stedingen">Stedingen</a>; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pope-gregory-ix">Pope Gregory IX</a> excommunicated him, and Frederick outlawed him on 5 July 1234. Henry revolted but was deserted by most of his followers and submitted to his father at Wimpfen on 2 July 1235. On 4 July 1235 Frederick and the princes tried Henry at Worms and dethroned him, and his brother Conrad was elected King of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-empire">Romans</a> in his place.</p><h2 class="enc-more-h">Death and legacy</h2><p>Henry was kept prisoner in several places, among them <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/heidelberg">Heidelberg</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/apulia">Apulia</a> and Rocca San Felice in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/campania">Campania</a>. Analysis of his skeleton in 1998 and 1999 showed that he had suffered from advanced leprosy in his last years, perhaps the reason the emperor never forgave him. He died near Martirano in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/calabria">Calabria</a> in February 1242 after a fall from his horse. He was buried with royal honours in the cathedral of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cosenza">Cosenza</a>. He is numbered only in parentheses, as he did not hold sole kingship, and was long disparaged as Parentheses Henry, though several historians have recently taken a more positive view of his policies.</p><p class="enc-more-src">This account follows the Wikipedia article “Henry (VII) of Germany” (CC BY-SA 4.0), linked under Read further below.</p></section>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>When the Gotthard Pass was opened to traffic in the early 13th century, the valley gained strategic value, and in 1231 King <b>Henry VII</b> bought it back from the Habsburgs and granted it imperial immediacy.</blockquote><a href="/state/canton-of-uri">Canton of Uri</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/palermo">Palermo</a>, in what is now <a href="/countries/italy">Italy</a>. Died in Martirano, in what is now <a href="/countries/italy">Italy</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=38.12,13.36&amp;year=1231" aria-label="Palermo on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4883 794 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the birthplace of Henry (VII) of Germany"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5333 1064h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5333 1064h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the birthplace. <a href="/atlas?at=38.12,13.36&amp;year=1231">What was here in 1231? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
